  "id": "schadenfreude",
  "term": "schadenfreude",
  "definition": "Schadenfreude is the feeling of pleasure, satisfaction, or grim enjoyment at another person’s misfortune. In psychology and ethics, it is viewed as a common but socially disapproved emotion that can be tied to motives such as envy, rivalry, or a sense that someone got what they deserved.",
